# Trivy ignore list — AlmaLinux 10 base (TICKET-020 / ADR-0069).
#
# This list is INTENTIONALLY EMPTY.
#
# It previously held ~90 Debian "trixie" base-image OS-package IDs that Trivy
# surfaced even though the Debian Security Tracker marked them "no fix planned /
# minor" — perma-noise with nothing to upgrade to. The migration to the
# AlmaLinux 10-minimal base (ADR-0069) removed the root cause:
#
#   * AlmaLinux ships authoritative OVAL/ALSA errata with backport-aware fixed
#     versions. The first Alma image scan (PR #17, 2026-06-20) confirmed it —
#     the remaining OS findings were openssl-libs CVEs, every one of which has
#     a FIXED VERSION available (1:3.5.5-4.el10_2.alma.1). Fixable findings are
#     resolved by rebuilding on the refreshed base, NOT by suppression.
#
# Policy: do NOT pre-populate this file. Suppress an EL/ALSA ID here only after
# evaluating a GENUINELY UNFIXABLE finding (Trivy reports an empty FixedVersion)
# that is also not reachable in this app's request path — with a one-line
# rationale per ID, the same narrow-scope discipline as before. Every new CVE,
# including new unfixable ones, must surface in CI and the Security tab until
# explicitly evaluated and added here. Keep the signal; drop only known noise.
